                <pb facs="0302" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg182"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Imperial edict of September 4, 1905.</hi></head>
                <p>A few days ago we issued an edict discontinuing the present system of
                    examinations and directing special attention to be given to the establishment of
                    schools.</p>
                <p>Let the literary chancellors in their provinces make it their special duty to
                    inspect the schools in their several provinces, and to consult with the viceroys
                    and governors concerned as to the management of educational affairs.</p>
            </div>
